 "findings": [
  "Gallagher is a genuine xG driver at 5v5 by both our model and an independent one: raw on-ice EV xGF/60 relative to his team +0.37 (2023-24) and +0.43 (2024-25), MoneyPuck 3-season 5on5 relative xGF/60 +0.59 (rank 20 of 564, Caufield +0.38, rank 59). His no-prior single-season RAPM was +0.28 / +0.36 in those years.",
  "2025-26 is the outlier year: on-ice rel -0.02, standalone +0.19 on 14.1 EV hours; his season-start prior (+0.52, SD 0.11, worth 24 EV hours) outweighs that season, so the posterior stays +0.475 (with his own prior reset it would be +0.16). This is the Kalman chain working as tuned: one weak 14-hour season against three strong ones.",
  "Collinearity is not the driver: his 2024-25/2025-26 linemates (Dvorak, Anderson, Danault, Carrier) are average-to-weak OFF players; Caufield shares 17-22 EV hours a season with Suzuki, which splits his on-ice credit (rel +0.53 every season, posterior +0.35).",
  "Loosening the prior does not lower him: the tuning-best looser chain (q_add 0.001) moves Gallagher UP to +0.505 because his strong 2023-25 data then count for more.",
  "What OFF misses is finishing. RAPM OFF is an xG impact by design. Gallagher has the 5th-worst shrunk finishing of all skaters with 20+ EV hours (FIN -0.145 goals/60: 190 EV goals on 229 league-scaled xG since 2010-11), Caufield the 11th best (+0.172: 128 on 101). OFF_total = OFF + FIN: Gallagher 0.33 (rank 52 of 564 qualified), Caufield 0.52 (rank 12)."
 ],
